Page 1295 viuda: Found match for regex: =
Page 1295 viuda: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{dercat|ca|itc-pro|ine-pro|inh=1}}
From {{der|ca|la|vidua}}.

In the Middle Ages, jurists introduced a learned Latin borrowing {{m|roa-oca|vídua}} to replace the inherited Old Catalan form {{m|roa-oca|viuva}} (from a Vulgar Latin {{m|la|*viduva}}). The current form {{m|ca||viuda}} supposedly emerged as a compromise between the two forms<ref>{{R:GDLC|viudo}}</ref>. The masculine form was derived from the feminine. Cf. also {{cog|es|viuda}}, which may have influenced it.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}

===Adjective===
{{head|ca|adjective form|g=f-s}}

# {{inflection of|ca|viudo||f|s}}

===Noun===
