{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|tartuga}} (cf. also earlier form {{m|roa-oca|tartaruga}}), probably from the feminine of {{inh|ca|LL.|Tartarucchus}} or {{m|la|tartarūchus}}, a mythological spirit of Greek origin, from {{der|ca|grc|ταρταροῦχος}}, from {{m|grc|Τάρταρος}}. Compare {{cog|oc|tartuga}}, {{cog|fr|tortue}}, {{cog|es|tortuga}}, {{cog|pt|tartaruga}}, {{cog|it|tartaruga}}. Cf. also Medieval Latin {{m|la|tortuca}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}
* {{audio|ca|LL-Q7026 (cat)-Millars-tortuga.wav|Audio (Valencian)}}

===Noun===
{{ca-noun|f}}

# [[turtle]]
# [[tortoise]]

