* {{alt|ca|avolla|avoia|voia||''from Vulgar Latin {{m|VL.||*ovuc(u)la}}''}}

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|oveylla}}, from {{inh|ca|la|ovicula}}, diminutive of {{m|la|ovis}}, from {{inh|ca|itc-pro|*owis}}, from {{inh|ca|ine-pro|*h₂ówis}}. Compare {{cog|oc|oelha}}. The initial diphthong in numerous regional variants reflects contamination from preceding determiners with final /-a/, as in {{m|ca||una ovella}} > {{m|ca||un' auvella}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA|ê}}
* {{audio|ca|LL-Q7026 (cat)-Unjoanqualsevol-ovella.wav|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{ca-noun|f}}

# [[sheep]]
#: {{syn|ca|be}}
# [[ewe]]

====Coordinate terms====
* {{l|ca|marrà}}
* {{l|ca|moltó}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ca|ovellenc}}
* {{l|ca|oveller}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ca|oví}}

===References===
* {{R:DCVB}}
* Petit Atles Lingüístic del Domini Català 6 [http://aldc.espais.iec.cat/files/2018/07/800-L_ovella.pdf 'ovella']

