===Etymology===
{{dercat|ca|qfa-sub}}
From {{der|ca|qfa-sub-ibe}}, possibly non-Indo-European. From the reconstructed term *''carapaccia'' (or *''calapaccia'': compare {{cog|es|calabaza}} and {{cog|pt|cabaça}}), denoting the envelope or shell of certain plants and animals. See also {{m|ca|clàpet}}. First attested in 1272.

