Page 6071 orxata: Found match for regex: =
Page 6071 orxata: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{der|ca|VL.|*hordeāta}}, itself derived from {{der|ca|la|hordeum|t=barley}}. How the word entered Catalan is disputed. Some see it as originating in the Valencian dialect (and making its way into Spanish ({{m|es|horchata}}) possibly via a Mozarabic source), but the word was only attested in Catalan around the 17th or 18th century, which makes this problematic. An alternatively etymology has the Catalan word borrowed from the {{der|ca|es|horchata}}, itself perhaps taken from the {{der|ca|it|orzata|t=barley water}}.<ref>{{R:GDLC}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}
* {{audio|ca|LL-Q7026 (cat)-Millars-orxata.wav|Audio (Valencian)}}

===Noun===
{{ca-noun|f}}

# [[horchata]] {{gloss|a sweet beverage}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ca|orxateria}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ca|ordi}}

===References===
<references/>

===Further reading===
* {{R:IEC2}}
* {{R:DNV}}
* {{R:DCVB}}

{{C|ca|Beverages}}
