Page 6162 enxaneta: Found match for regex: =
Page 6162 enxaneta: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Uncertain, 19th century. The following have been proposed:
# from {{der|ca|oc|*enjaneta}}, diminutive of {{der|ca|oc|engana|t=arrow, steeple}};
# diminutive of {{m|ca|genet|t=rider}}, since the enxaneta straddles the {{l|ca|acotxador}};
# variant of {{m|ca|angelet|t=little angel}}, from the origins of castells in the figures built in the ''ball de valencians'' to represent various religious scenes, in this case the [[w:Assumption of Mary|Assumption of Mary]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{ca-noun|mfbysense}}

# {{lb|ca|castells}} the person, typically a child, who forms the top of a [[castell]]
-------- end text --------
