===Etymology===
From {{der|ca|la|subtrahō||to remove}}, with the first syllable altered by analogy with words like {{m|ca|sosllevar}} and {{m|ca|soscavar}} which contain a prefix derived from the archaic preposition {{m|ca|sots}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA|è}}

===Verb===
{{ca-verb|pres_1_sg=sostrec|past_part=sostret}}

# {{lb|ca|transitive}} to [[remove]], to [[relieve]], to [[take away]]
#: {{ux|ca|Res no podrà '''sostreure''' a l’esser humà de les tristes condicions de la seva existència: patir i morir.|Nothing will be able to '''relieve''' human beings of the sad conditions of their existence: to suffer and die.}}
# {{lb|ca|arithmetic|transitive}} to [[subtract]]
# {{lb|ca|transitive}} to [[steal]]
# {{lb|ca|pronominal}} to [[steal away]], to [[get away]] {{q|from ''a''}}, to [[evade]], to [[resist]]
#: {{ux|ca|Em vaig poder '''sostreure''' a l'entorn hostil que hi havia.|I was able to '''escape''' the hostile environment that was there.}}

