# {{lb|ca|music}} {{l|en|mi}} (third note of diatonic scale)

===Etymology 3===

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|f}}

# [[mu]]; the [[Appendix:Greek script|Greek alphabet]] letter [[Μ]] (lowercase [[μ]])

===Etymology 4===

====Verb====
{{head-lite|ca|verb forms}}
# {{lb|ca|colloquial}} {{ca-verb form of|p=2|n=sg|m=impr|mirar}}

=====Usage notes=====
This form is an optional reduced form of the imperative {{m-lite|ca|mira}} that can see use when combined with one or more clitic pronouns attached to the end of the verb - for example:
* {{m-lite|ca||mi-}}{{m-lite|ca|te}}{{m-lite|ca|'l||look at it, look at him}} for {{m-lite|ca||mira-}}{{m-lite|ca|te}}{{m-lite|ca|'l}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{qualifier-lite|Algherese}} {{l-lite|ca|mi-lo}}, {{l-lite|ca|mi-la}}, {{l-lite|ca|mi-los}}, {{l-lite|ca|mi-les}} {{gloss-lite|behold!, here it is!, here they are!}}

