# {{lb|ca|intransitive}} to [[take]] a long time, to [[be long]]
# {{lb|ca|intransitive}} to be [[late]]
# {{lb|ca|transitive}} to [[take]] (a certain amount of time)

====Usage notes====
The main difference between {{m|ca|trigar}} and {{m|ca|durar}} when used transitively is that the former signifies some event that one has to wait for, while the latter signifies an ongoing action.

