===Etymology===
Apparently from dialectal {{m|ca|trapitx||olive oil press}}, which may represent a Mozarabic development of {{der|ca|gkm|*τραπήτιον}}, a diminutive of {{m|la|trapētus}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}
* {{rhymes|ca|a(ɾ)|s=3}}

===Verb===
{{ca-verb}}
# to [[tread]] on, to [[step]] on
#: {{syn|ca|petjar|peucalcigar}}
#* {{RQ:Sanchez Pell freda | chapter = 5 | passage = Amb la bota vaig '''trepitjar''' el peu despullat, udols de dolor van escampar-se pel bosc. | translation = With my boot I '''stepped on''' the shoeless foot; screams of pain filled the woods.}}
# to [[crush]] underfoot, [[trample]]
#: {{syn|ca|esclafar|trepollar}}
# {{lb|ca|winemaking}} to [[tread]] grapes to make wine
#: {{syn|ca|follar}}
# {{lb|ca|figurative}} to [[trample]], to [[walk all over]]

