Page 16161 anar: Found match for regex: =
Page 16161 anar: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From early {{inh|ca|ML.|andāre}}, of uncertain origin.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}
* {{audio|ca|LL-Q7026 (cat)-Unjoanqualsevol-anar.wav|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{ca-verb|pres_1_sg=vaig}}

# to [[go]]
# {{lb|ca|auxiliary verb, taking an infinitive}} {{ngd|forms the periphrastic preterite; see usage notes below for more information}}
#: {{ux|ca|Ahir '''vaig''' parlar amb ma germana.|Yesterday, I spoke with my sister.}}

====Usage notes====
The second set of conjugations are used along with the infinitive of another verb in order to form the "{{glossary|periphrastic}} past" (''passat perifràstic''), an analytical construction equivalent in terms of tense and aspect to the simple preterite. For example, ''vaig cantar'' bears the same meaning as ''cantí'' ('I sang').

The indicative forms of the auxiliary, except for the third-person singular, may be reinforced with -''re''-, but, in the standard language, only when the corresponding normal first-conjugation simple preterite endings have it. For example, the standard language permits ''vares cantar'' for use instead of ''vas cantar'' but not *''vàreig cantar'' instead of ''vaig cantar''; compare the typical second-person singular ending -''a'''re'''s'' with its first-person singular equivalent -''í''. The subjunctive forms are literary and only sporadically occur, and so rather than the periphrastic past subjunctive, it is typical for the imperfect subjunctive to be used (therefore ''cantés'' rather than ''vagi cantar'', for example), despite the demand for the perfective aspect.

====Conjugation====
{{ca-conj-anar}}
{{ca-conj-anar-pp-aux|dialect=Central Catalan|vaig|vas|ind_2_sg_alt=vares|va|vam|ind_1_pl_alt=vàrem|vau|ind_2_pl_alt=vàreu|van|ind_3_pl_alt=varen|vagi|vagis|vagi|vàgim|vàgiu|vagin}}
{{ca-conj-anar-pp-aux|dialect=Valencian|vaig|vas|ind_2_sg_alt=vares|va|vam|ind_1_pl_alt=vàrem|vau|ind_2_pl_alt=vàreu|van|ind_3_pl_alt=varen|vaja|vages|vaja|vàgem|vàgeu|vagen}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ca|anada}}
* {{l|ca|anar a mal borràs}}
* {{l|ca|anar a parar}}
* {{l|ca|anar-se'n}}

