Page 16208 estrenar: -------- begin text --------
{{was fwotd|ca|2018|October|26}}

===Etymology===
From {{af|ca|estrena|-ar|t1=premiere}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}
* {{rhymes|ca|a(ɾ)|s=3}}

===Verb===
{{ca-verb}}

# {{lb|ca|transitive}} to [[wear]] or [[use]] for the first time
#* {{quote-text|ca|year=2010|author=Maria Barbal|title=La pressa del temps
|passage=Estudien, treballen, es casen, arreglen la casa, surten amb amics, es cuiden i '''estrenen''' roba sovint, tenen temps per a tot, per a cada cosa.
|translation=They study, they work, they get married, they tidy up the house, they go out with friends, they take care of each other and they '''wear''' new clothes often, they have time for everything, for each and every thing.}}
# {{lb|ca|by extension|transitive}} to [[premiere]] {{gloss|to present a play or film for the first time}}
#* {{quote-journal|ca|title='Orange is the new black' acabarà després de la setena temporada|journal=Ara|date=Oct 18 2018|passage=El drama carcerari, que es va '''estrenar''' el 2013, començava amb l'entrada a la presó de Piper Chapman (Taylor Schilling), {{...}}|translation=The prison drama, which '''premiered''' in 2013, began with the entrance into prison of Piper Chapman (Taylor Schilling) {{...}}|url=https://www.ara.cat/media/Orange-acabara-despres-setena-temporada_0_2108789302.html}}
# {{lb|ca|reflexive|estrenar-se}} to do something for the first time; to [[break one's duck]]
# {{lb|ca|reflexive|estrenar-se}} to make the first sale of the day

====Conjugation====
{{ca-conj-ar|estren}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:IEC2}}
* {{R:GDLC}}
* {{R:DNV}}
* {{R:DCVB}}

