{{inh+|ca|VL.|*virō|*virāre}}, probably from {{der|ca|la|vibrō|vibrāre}} (in which case it is a {{doublet|ca|vibrar|nocap=1}}). Other possibilities include an alteration of {{m|la|gȳrō}} (source of the synonym {{m|ca|girar}}) or a derivation from {{cog|cel-gau|*viru|t=to deviate, veer off}}, itself derived from {{m|cel-gau|viros|t=round, crooked}}. Compare {{cog|it|virare}}, {{cog|fr|virer}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}

