Page 16816 resar: Found match for regex: =
Page 16816 resar: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{bor+|ca|es|rezar}}, from {{der|ca|la|recito|recītāre|t=recite}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}
* {{rhymes|ca|a(ɾ)|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{ca-verb}}

# to [[pray]]
# to [[officiate]] in a religious service

====Usage notes====
In its original sense, {{m|ca|resar}} meant to read an oration: hence a {{m|ca|missa resada}} is a mass which is read rather than sung ("low mass"). It has come to be used in the sense of to pray, especially when referring to non-Christian religions, in preference to the verb {{m|ca|pregar}}, which has taken on a more mundane sense.

====Conjugation====
{{ca-conj-ar|res}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ca|missa resada}} {{g|f}}
* {{l|ca|rés}} {{g|m}}

===References===
* {{R:DCVB}}
-------- end text --------
Page 16817 fresar: Found match for regex: =
Page 16817 fresar: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|ca|VL.|*frictiare}}, from {{der|ca|la|fricō|fricāre|to rub}}. Originally this described the action of some animals who rub their bellies on the ground while laying eggs and from there was extended to "lay eggs, spawn" in general. {{doublet|ca|fressar}}.

====Verb====
{{ca-verb}}

# {{lb|ca|intransitive}} to [[spawn]]
# {{lb|ca|intransitive}} to [[defecate]] {{q|of rabbits, etc.}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ca|fres}}
* {{l|ca|fresa}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{af|ca|fresa|-ar|t1=milling cutter}}.

====Verb====
{{ca-verb}}

# {{lb|ca|transitive}} to [[mill]] (using a [[milling cutter]])
# {{lb|ca|transitive}} to [[mix]] [[flour]] with water before [[kneading]]

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ca|fresatge}}

===Conjugation===
{{ca-conj-ar|fres}}

