Page 18164 ser: Found match for regex: =
Page 18164 ser: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ca|ésser}}

===Etymology===
From a reduction of {{m|ca|ésser}}, from {{inh|ca|la|sum}}, from {{inh|ca|itc-pro|*ezom}}, from {{inh|ca|ine-pro|*h₁ésti||to be, to exist}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|ca|LL-Q7026 (cat)-Unjoanqualsevol-ser.wav|Audio}}
{{q|verb}}
* {{ca-IPA}}
{{q|noun}}
* {{ca-IPA|sérr}}

===Verb===
{{ca-verb|pres_1_sg=sóc|past_part=estat}}

# {{lb|ca|intransitive}} to [[be]], to [[exist]]
#: {{ux|ca|'''Ser''' o no '''ser''', aquesta és la qüestió.|To '''be''' or not to '''be''', that is the question.}}
# {{lb|ca|intransitive|+adverbial phrase}} to be [[located]] {{gloss|to be in a place}}
# {{lb|ca|transitive|copular}} to [[be]] {{gloss|used to connect a noun to another noun}}
# {{lb|ca|transitive|copular}} to [[have]] a [[characteristic]] {{gloss|used to connect a noun to an adjective that describes an inherent property}}
# {{lb|ca|auxiliary}} {{non-gloss definition|forms the [[passive voice]], together with a [[past participle]]}}

====Usage notes====
This is one of two verbs that can be translated as ''to be'', the other being {{m|ca|estar}}. ''Ser/ésser'' indicates an inherent quality, whereas ''estar'' indicates temporary qualities that apply only at a particular time. ''Ser/ésser'' relates to ''estar'' as {{m|en|essence}} relates to {{m|en|state}}, etymologically as well as semantically.

