Page 20585 escocès: Found match for regex: =
Page 20585 escocès: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ca|escocés||Valencian}}

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|ca|Escòcia|ès|gloss1=Scotland}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}

===Adjective===
{{ca-adj}}

# [[Scottish]] {{gloss|pertaining to Scotland, the Scottish people, or the Scottish language}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ca|anglès escocès}}
* {{l|ca|anglés escocès}}

===Noun===
{{ca-noun|m|f=escocesa}}

# [[Scot]]; [[Scotsman]] {{gloss|an inhabitant of Scotland}}

====Synonyms====
* {{qualifier|archaic}} {{l|ca|escot}}

===Noun===
{{ca-noun|m|-}}

# [[Scots]] {{gloss|language}}
# [[Scottish Gaelic]] {{gloss|language}}
#: {{syn|ca|gaèlic escocès}}
# [[Scottish English]] {{gloss|dialect}}
#: {{syn|ca|anglès escocès}}

====Usage notes====
By itself, {{m|ca||escocès}} usually indicates Scots, but context may indicate a different sense or even a combination of senses. In older texts, {{m|ca||escocès}} would be more likely to refer to Scottish Gaelic than to Scots. The use of {{m|ca||escocès}} for Scottish English usually only occurs among those who consider Scots to be an English dialect rather than a language of its own.

{{C|ca|Demonyms|Dialects|Languages|Nationalities}}
-------- end text --------
Page 20586 gaèlic escocès: Found match for regex: =
Page 20586 gaèlic escocès: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ca|gaèlic escocés||Valencian}}

===Noun===
{{ca-noun|m|-}}

# [[Scottish Gaelic]] {{gloss|language}}
#: {{syn|ca|escocès}}

====Usage notes====
* For the sake of clarity, this term is preferred today to its synonym {{m|ca|escocès}}, which can have several meanings, of which Scottish Gaelic is not the predominant one.
* Unlike English in which Gaelic is considered a synonym of Scottish Gaelic, in Catalan, {{m|ca|gaèlic||Gaelic}} is a synonym of {{m|ca|gaèlic irlandès||Irish Gaelic}}.

{{C|ca|Languages}}
