===Etymology 1===
From {{af|ca|lleganya|-ós}}.

====Adjective====
{{ca-adj}}

# {{q|of eyes}} [[rheumy]], full of [[sleep]] or [[crusties]]
#* {{quote-book|ca|year=1956|author=Joan Sales|title=Incerta glòria|text=¿I la tia Olegària? Dels ullets vermells i '''lleganyosos''' queien unes llàgrimes com cigrons.|t=And Aunt Olegària? From her little red and '''rheumy''' eyes fell tears like chickpeas.}}
# having eyes full of [[sleep]] or [[crusties]]

===Etymology 2===
From {{af|ca|llegany|-ós}}.

====Adjective====
{{ca-adj}}

# full of thin clouds which allow sunshine to penetrate
#* {{quote-book|ca|year=2005|title=A Jerusalem|author=Josep Piera|text=El dia s'ha despertat gris, '''lleganyós''', com si volgués ploure; o com si el cel estigués tan desvalgut com tots, sense saber ni plorar una llàgrima.|t=The had broken grey, '''with light clouds''', as if it wanted to rain, or as if the sky were as helpless as everyone, not even knowing how to cry a tear.}}

