Page 23133 cent: Found match for regex: {
Page 23133 cent: -------- begin text --------
{{number box|ca}}

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|ca|la|centum}}, from {{inh|ca|itc-pro|*kentom}}, from {{inh|ca|ine-pro|*ḱm̥tóm}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{a|Standard}}
:* (before the words "anys", "homes", "hores") {{IPA|ca|/ˈsent/}}
:* (any other position) {{IPA|ca|/ˈsen/}}
* {{a|Valencian}} and {{a|Balearic}} {{IPA|ca|/ˈsent/}}
* {{homophones|ca|sent}}
* {{rhymes|ca|ent|s=1}}

====Numeral====
{{ca-num}}

# {{lb|ca|cardinal}} [[hundred]]

=====Usage notes=====
{{U:ca:cardinal numbers}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ca|cent per cent}}
* {{l|ca|per cent}}

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|m}}

# [[hundred]]

====See also====
* {{l|ca|dos-cents|g=m|t=two hundred}}, {{l|ca|dues-centes|g=f|t=two hundred}}
** Old Catalan: {{l|ca|doents|t=two hundred}}
* {{l|ca|tres-cents|t=three hundred}}
* {{l|ca|quatre-cents|t=four hundred}}
* {{l|ca|cinc-cents|t=five hundred}}
* {{l|ca|sis-cents|t=six hundred}}
* {{l|ca|set-cents|t=seven hundred}}
* {{l|ca|vuit-cents|t=eight hundred}}
* {{l|ca|nou-cents|t=nine hundred}}

===Etymology 2===
{{bor+|ca|en|cent}}. These senses of the word ''cent'' in Catalan derive from the inversion of meaning that took place in English where it was used to indicate one hundredth.

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|m}}

# {{lb|ca|music}} {{l|en|cent}} {{gloss|a hundredth of a [[half step]]}}
# {{lb|ca|money}} {{l|en|cent}} {{gloss|a [[subunit]] of currency equal to one-hundredth of the [[euro]]}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|ca|cèntim||a [[subunit]] of currency equal to one-hundredth of the base unit}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:IEC2}}
* {{R:GDLC}}
* {{R:DNV}}
* {{R:DCVB}}

