Page 25135 meu: Found match for regex: =
Page 25135 meu: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|ca|roa-oca|meu}}, from {{inh|ca|la|meus|meum}}, from {{inh|ca|itc-pro|*meos}}. The feminine form was {{m|roa-oca|mia}} in Old Catalan, but this was extended to {{m|ca|meva}} or {{m|ca|meua}} by analogy with the masculine form. This happened because the ''-u'' was not understood as a masculine ending anymore, having been lost in nouns (unlike Spanish, Portuguese and Italian {{m|und||-o}}).

The weak possessive {{m|ca|mon}} is also from {{inh|ca|la|meus|meum}}, but as an unstressed monosyllabic form.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ca-IPA|é}}

====Pronoun====
{{head|ca|pronoun|cat2=possessive pronouns|feminine|meva|or|meua|masculine plural|meus|feminine plural|meves|or|meues}}

# [[my]], [[mine]]

=====Usage notes=====
* When preceding a noun, {{m|ca||meu}} is always preceded by the appropriate definite article.
*: {{uxi|ca|'''el''' meu gos|my dog}}
* Also used after some prepositions:
*: {{uxi|ca|dins '''meu'''|inside '''me'''}}
*: {{uxi|ca|davant '''meu'''|in front of '''me'''}}

=====Declension=====
{{ca-decl-ppron}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|ca|mon}}

===Etymology 2===

====Pronunciation====
* {{ca-IPA|è}}

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|m}}

# {{lb|ca|2016 spelling reform}} {{alternative form of|ca|mèu|t=meow}}

===Etymology 3===
{{bor+|ca|la|mēum}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ca-IPA|è}}

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|m}}

# [[baldmoney]], [[spignel]]

===Further reading===
* {{R:IEC2}}
* {{R:DCVB}}

{{C|ca|Selineae tribe plants}}

