Page 26305 -è: Found match for regex: =
Page 26305 -è: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ca|-é||Valencia}}

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ca|la|-ēnus}}, from {{m|la|-nus}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}

===Suffix===
{{ca-adj}}

# {{n-g|forms an ordinal number from a cardinal number}}
# {{lb|ca|chemistry}} [[-ene]]

====Usage notes====
The first four ordinals are irregular, and irregular forms derived directly from the Latin ordinal instead of using this suffix on the modern Catalan cardinal exist for 5, 6, 7, 8, 10, 20, 100, and 1000. Ordinals for the powers of 1 000 000 do not use this suffix, but instead use {{m|ca|-èsim}}. Uniquely, {{m|ca|novè||ninth}} can be viewed as either coming from the use of this suffix or directly from the Latin ordinal.

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|ca}}

-------- end text --------
Page 26306 1000è: Found match for regex: =
Page 26306 1000è: -------- begin text --------

===Adjective===
{{head|ca|adjective|feminine|1000a|g=m}}

# [[1000th]] ; {{abbreviation of|ca|milè}}

====Usage notes====
While {{m|ca|mil·lèsim}} is the more commonly used term for {{m|en|thousandth}}, the masculine ordinal abbreviation is derived from the term derived from {{m|ca|mil||thousand}} + {{m|ca|-è||masculine ordinal suffix}} in common with all the masculine ordinals after the first four ({{m|ca|1r||1st}}, {{m|ca|2n||2nd}}, {{m|ca|3r||3rd}}, {{m|ca|4t||4th}}, ).
-------- end text --------
