Page 26985 romaní: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|ca|la|rosmarīnus}}. Compare {{cog|oc|romanin}}.

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|m}}

# [[rosemary]]
#: {{syn|ca|romer|q1=dialectal}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ca|romaní bord}}
* {{l|ca|romaní mascle}}

===Etymology 2===

====Adjective====
{{ca-adj|mf|pl=romanís|pl2=romanins}}

# [[Romani]] {{gloss|pertaining to the Roma people or to the Romani languages}}
#: {{syn|ca|gitano}}

====Noun====
{{head|ca|noun|plural|romanís|Valencian plural|romanins|g=mf}}

# [[Roma]] {{gloss|a member of the Roma people}}
#: {{syn|ca|gitano}}

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|m|-}}

# [[Romani]] {{gloss|a family of Indo-Aryan languages used by the Roma people of Europe}}
#: {{syn|ca|gitano}}
#: {{hypo|ca|caló}}

====Usage notes====
* The term {{m|ca||romaní|Romany, Roma}} is of recent coinage in Catalan, reflecting the {{glossary|endonym}} of the Roma. The older {{glossary|exonym}}, {{m|ca|gitano||Gypsy}}, is still popular.
* The {{m|ca|IEC}} and {{m|ca|AVL}} disagree over the proper plural of {{m|ca||romaní}}. The AVL has chosen to prescribe the regular plural {{m|ca||romanins}} as if the term had a Latin derivation, while the IEC has chosen to prescribe the plural form {{m|ca||romanís}}.

===References===
