===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA}}
* {{rhymes|ca|o|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
Of {{unk|ca|nocap=1}} origin. Suggestions have included Proto-Indo-European {{m|ine-pro|*bekione||double, partner}}, {{der|ca|la||*bissōne|double}}, and a pre-Roman *''bikione'' related to {{m+|eu|biki||twin}}, {{m|eu|biko||pair}}, and {{m|eu|bikun||double}}. Compare {{cog|frp|besson}},  {{cog|oc|besson}} and {{cog|pms|bësson}}

====Adjective====
[[File:Conjoined cherries.jpg|thumb|''una cirera bessona''<br>a conjoined cherry]]
{{ca-adj}}

# [[twin]]
# {{lb|ca|botany|relational}} of [[conjoin]]ed fruits that are usually separate

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ca|arbre bessó}}
* {{l|ca|espelta bessona|t=emmer}}

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|m|f=bessona}}

# [[twin]]

===Etymology 2===
Probably from a semantic variation of {{m|ca|[[ametlla]] [[bessona]]|t=conjoined almond}}.

====Noun====
{{ca-noun|m}}

# the [[meat]] of a nut; especially an almond
# the [[meat]] of a fruit or vegetable
# [[bone marrow]]
# the [[meat]] or [[essence]] of something

